        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "1-Amino-2-naphthol hydrochloride (0.10 mmol), 2-hydroxy-1-naphthaldehyde (0.10 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.10 mmol), CH3OH (0.75 mL), and CH3CN (0.75 mL) were added in a Pyrex tube, then 2-picolylamine (45 μL) was dropped in. After reaction at 80 °C for 48 h, the mixture was cooled slowly to obtain red block crystals.",
